# Two env files, one per process that reads secrets. Never commit them.
#
#   cp .env.example agent/.env     → the Claude Agent SDK agent (FastAPI, :8000)
#   cp .env.example backend/.env   → the Copilot Runtime (Node, :8200)
#
# Each process ignores the variables meant for the other. The Vite frontend
# reads none of these and never sees a key.

# ── agent/.env — loaded by main.py itself (load_dotenv), as the Quickstart's ──
# ── own .env step sets up                                                    ──

# Required. Read by the Claude Agent SDK (via the environment) for every run.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The Quickstart's model; main.py falls back to the same value if unset.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8

# ── backend/.env — read by `npm run dev` in backend/ ────────────────────────

# Required. Where the landing page's HttpAgent reaches the agent: the Claude
# Agent SDK Quickstart serves it at POST "/" on :8000 (uvicorn ... --port 8000).
AGENT_URL=http://localhost:8000/

# Optional. Runtime port; the Vite proxy targets 8200, so change both together.
# PORT=8200

# Optional. CopilotKit Intelligence project key, for /api/copilotkit-threads
# only (Threads Drawer, Headless Threads), wired per
# https://docs.copilotkit.ai/vue/claude-sdk-python/intelligence/quickstart.
#   cd backend && npx copilotkit@latest login && npx copilotkit@latest project select
# Without it that runtime is plain SSE (no thread store). Server-side only.
# CPK_INTELLIGENCE_API_KEY=cpk-...

# Optional. The fixed local identity the Threads runtime gives every caller.
# NOT authentication.
# APP_USER_ID=local-user

# Optional. MCP server for /generative-ui/mcp-apps (`npm run mcp:apps` in backend/).
# MCP_APPS_URL=http://localhost:3101/mcp

# Optional. Opt out of CopilotKit runtime telemetry.
# COPILOTKIT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=true
